on a topic node to show strategies, then switch to '⚔️ Battle Arena' to show the Golem Boss fight]Speaker 3:"Let’s look at the application in action. When a student first launches FocusFlow, they go through a diagnostic setup that maps out their individual learning profile.   Look at this Neural Brain Map. Each node represents a subject or topic. Green nodes show mastered strengths, while red or highlighted nodes flag friction traps that need attention. Students can click any neuron to instantly launch targeted timers or subject battles.   Now, watch what happens when we enter the Battle Arena to face The Fraction Golem. Instead of mindless button-mashing, defeating the boss requires answering real curriculum questions—like simplifying fractions. Every correct answer deals a critical hit to the enemy, earns XP, and levels up the hero. If they struggle, they can use tactical abilities like 'Insight' or 'Guard' powered by focus energy. Learning is literally woven into gameplay!"   Speaker 4: Live Demonstration — Flashcards & Kanban Planner (3 Minutes)[Screen Action: Switch to '🎴 Recall Decks', show note parsing/PDF upload, then switch to '📋 Kanban']Speaker 4:"But FocusFlow isn't just an RPG game; it's a complete academic toolkit.   In the Recall Decks tab, students can paste their raw study notes or upload class PDFs directly. The app automatically parses the text and extracts key definitions into 3D flippable flashcards for active recall.   Once those concepts are reviewed, students manage their daily workload using our Neubrutalist Kanban Planner. Notice how quests from the RPG can be exported directly as tasks onto the Kanban board, moving smoothly from To Do to In Progress to Mastered. Combined with our Hyper-Pomodoro Arcade Timer, students have a complete ecosystem to structure their day without losing track of their goals."   Speaker 5: Wellbeing Connection, Practical Application & Conclusion (2.5 Minutes)[Screen Action: Open the Pitch Modal or return to the main dashboard overview]Speaker 5:"How does this support our school wellbeing? This directly aligns with the Psychological Wellbeing SPIRE pillar by fostering a sense of academic agency and reducing anxiety. By breaking massive exam syllabi into bite-sized quests, students replace late-night cramming panic with positive reinforcement, structure, and emotional balance.   How can students use it regularly at school?During morning study periods, they can review 5 minutes of flashcards from their Recall Decks.   During homework blocks, they use the 25-minute Pomodoro timer for deep work and manage tasks on the Kanban board.   Before tests, they run revision sprints in the Dungeon to patch up weak spots.   To conclude, our team believes in one powerful message: Studying for exams doesn't have to feel like an uphill battle against burnout. By turning education into an adventure where curiosity is rewarded and friction is conquered, FocusFlow empowers every student to take charge of their learning and thrive.   Thank you! We'd love to answer any questions you have."
